    public static void main(String args[]) {
        StringBuffer sb = new StringBuffer("Hello");   //String literal stored in SCP
        sb.append(" Hi");                              //content can be modified as StringBuffer is mutable
        System.out.println(sb);
    }
}

| Method                  | Purpose                               | Example                          | Return Type  |
|-------------------------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-------------|
| append()                | Add data at end                       | sb.append("Java");               | StringBuffer|
| insert()                | Insert data at specified index        | sb.insert(5, "Java");            | StringBuffer|
| delete()                | Delete characters between indexes     | sb.delete(0, 5);                 | StringBuffer|
| replace()               | Replace characters                    | sb.replace(0, 5, "Hi");          | StringBuffer|
| reverse()               | Reverse the StringBuffer              | sb.reverse();                    | StringBuffer|
| length()                | Returns number of characters          | sb.length();                     | int         |
| capacity()              | Returns current capacity              | sb.capacity();                   | int         |
| charAt()                | Returns character at given index      | sb.charAt(1);                    | char        |
| setCharAt()             | Modify character at given index       | sb.setCharAt(0, 'H');            | void        |
| indexOf()               | Returns first occurrence index        | sb.indexOf("Java");              | int         |
| lastIndexOf()           | Returns last occurrence index         | sb.lastIndexOf("Java");          | int         |
| substring(beginIndex)   | Returns substring from index          | sb.substring(2);                 | String      |
| substring(begin,end)    | Returns substring between indexes     | sb.substring(1, 4);              | String      |
| toString()              | Converts StringBuffer to String       | sb.toString();                   | String      |

StringBuilder:It is predefined class available in java.lang package, mutable sequence of character, but not thread-safe
-------------
- StringBuilder provides an API compatible with StringBuffer.
- Unlike StringBuffer, it does not guarantee synchronization.
- Designed as a drop-in replacement for StringBuffer when only a single thread is used.
- Recommended over StringBuffer in single-threaded applications because of better performance
- Available from 1.5v of Java 
class SBDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        StringBuilder sb =
            new StringBuilder("Hello");

        sb.append(" Java");

        System.out.println(sb);
    }
}

| Method                  | Purpose                               | Example                          | Return Type  |
|-------------------------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------|-------------|
| append()                | Add data at end                       | sb.append("Java");               | StringBuilder |
| insert()                | Insert data at specified index        | sb.insert(5, "Java");            | StringBuilder |
| delete()                | Delete characters between indexes     | sb.delete(0, 5);                 | StringBuilder |
| replace()               | Replace characters                    | sb.replace(0, 5, "Hi");          | StringBuilder |
| reverse()               | Reverse the StringBuilder             | sb.reverse();                    | StringBuilder |
| length()                | Returns number of characters          | sb.length();                     | int         |
| capacity()              | Returns current capacity              | sb.capacity();                   | int         |
| charAt()                | Returns character at given index      | sb.charAt(1);                    | char        |
| setCharAt()             | Modify character at given index       | sb.setCharAt(0, 'H');            | void        |
| indexOf()               | Returns first occurrence index        | sb.indexOf("Java");              | int         |
| lastIndexOf()           | Returns last occurrence index         | sb.lastIndexOf("Java");          | int         |
| substring(beginIndex)   | Returns substring from index          | sb.substring(2);                 | String      |
